INSTALL
  1. adb install -r -t app-debug.apk
     -> FAILURE [INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE: Existing package
        com.example.guidedogtest signatures do not match newer version]
     The copy already on the phone was built with a DIFFERENT debug keystore
     (~/.android/debug.keystore is per machine), so it cannot be updated in place.
  2. Checked for app-owned data before removing it:
       adb shell run-as com.example.guidedogtest ls shared_prefs
     -> only com.google.* (Maps/MLKit/geo SDK) and settings_preference.xml; there was NO
        motor-settings.xml, i.e. this phone had never saved any tuning. Nothing to lose.
  3. adb uninstall com.example.guidedogtest   -> Success
  4. adb install -r app-debug.apk             -> Success   (15.6 s, streamed)
  Note for the team: installing from a different laptop hits the same conflict. Either
  uninstall first, or keep one machine as the one that installs.

